jobs.description:
IRCCS San Raffaele Scientific Institute in Milan, Italy, is looking for a highly motived and qualified Lab technician to join the Genome Editing and Clonal Dynamics of Hematopoiesis Unit (SR-Tiget), opening in January 2027, led by Dr. Samuele Ferrari.


**The Institute:** SR-Tiget was created in 1996 as a joint-venture between Fondazione Telethon and Ospedale San Raffaele (OSR), with the mission to perform cutting edge research on gene and cell therapy and to translate its results into therapeutic advances for genetic diseases. The Institute is located within the OSR campus, which includes a large multi-disciplinary research hospital, a biomedical research center, a university and also hosts several biotechnologies companies. Over the years, SR-Tiget has given a pioneering contribution to the gene and cell therapy field with relevant discoveries in vector design, gene transfer and gene editing strategies, stem cell biology, identity and mechanism of action of regulatory cells in immune responses and innate immune cells in cancer. SR-Tiget has also established the resources and framework for translating these advances into novel experimental therapies and has implemented several successful gene therapy clinical trials, which have already treated >150 patients and led to the filing and approval of 3 novel advanced therapy medicines.


**The Unit:** In few words: edit, trace, understand, cure. The Genome Editing and Clonal Dynamics of Hematopoiesis Unit investigates how genetic alterations shape hematopoietic stem cell function, clonal evolution, and disease development. By combining genome editing, stem cell biology, and advanced omics for lineage tracing in humans, we aim to understand the mechanisms that govern the emergence, selection, and behavior of hematopoietic clones in health and disease. A major focus of the laboratory is the study of acquired genetic disorders, with VEXAS syndrome serving as a compelling paradigm for understanding how somatic mutations drive clonal hematopoiesis, cellular adaptation, systemic inflammation, and disease progression. Ultimately, by integrating mechanistic studies with the development and application of genome editing technologies, we aim to identify opportunities for precision treatments, including gene therapies.


**The team:** the successful candidate will work in a multidisciplinary, committed, and enthusiastic team of scientists with background in genome editing and stem cell biology, including post-doctoral researchers, hematologists, PhD and graduate students. The team members have frequent scientific interactions with OSR clinical units and SR-Tiget bioinformaticians, as well as with OSR and external collaborators.

**Project number:** SR-Tiget Core Grant

**Project Title:** Studying VEXAS as a paradigm of clonal hematopoiesis


**Main responsibilities:**  
Efficiently prioritize and execute technical duties and biomedical experiments;

Prepare samples for omics profiling and flow cytometry;

Isolate, manipulate, and culture human primary cells;

Execute molecular and cell biology techniques;

Produce and employ lentiviral vectors and gene editing reagents;

Interaction with the staff from other units and areas within SR-Tiget (in particular “Research Operations”).


The candidate we are looking for has the following qualifications and skills:

Master’s degree in biology, biotechnology or similar;

Previous and continuous experience in biomedical/molecular biology research;

Experience in molecular biology, flow cytometry, and cell culture;

Previous experience in gene and cell therapies (including viral vector preparation), stem cell culture and manipulation, library preparation for omic technologies, genome editing, and animal handling are a plus;

Pro-active, collaborative, and committed mindset;

Ability to prioritize and manage multiple tasks and to work in team;

Good communication skills in English.


**What we offer:**  
**Type of contract:** full-time fixed-term contract;

**Range Gross Annual Salary:** € 26,000-35,000 depending on experience and seniority;

**Duration:** 1 year, renewable;

**Place of work:** IRCCS San Raffaele Hospital, Via Olgettina, number 60 - Milan (Italy).


Selected references



* Canarutto, Fiumara et al, Nature Biotechnology 2026 – PMID: 42225947
* Beck et al, Nature Review Disease Primers 2026 – PMID: 41991535
* Molteni, Fiumara et al, Nature Medicine 2025 – PMID: 40195449
* Fiumara, Ferrari et al, Nature Biotechnology 2023 – PMID: 37679541
* Vavassori, Ferrari et al, Blood 2023 – PMID: 37294917
* Ferrari, Jacob, Cesana et al, Cell Stem Cell 2023 – PMID: 36206730
* Ferrari, Jacob et al, Nature Biotechnology 2020 – PMID: 32601433

At San Raffaele Scientific Institute, a world-renowned center of excellence for clinical and scientific activities, we believe that considering diversity and promoting an open and inclusive environment is crucial to our success. We are committed to ensure that equal employment opportunities are provided and based on merit without regard to age, religion, sex, disability, medical condition, sexual orientation, cultural and social backgrounds, gender identity or expression, national or ethnic origin, or any other legally recognized status entitled to protection under applicable laws. We offer attractive conditions and rewards appropriate to an internationally competitive research organization.

